# Mobile CI/CD — Start Here

This section applies the new Master Handbook together with the earlier governed Build & Release Kit and workshop. It takes an Android, iOS, or React Native application from repository preparation to **verified delivery**. Bitrise builds the app; required test/security gates control progression; the approved destination makes the version available to its intended users.

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing files, private binaries, and sensitive logs in approved Enterprise systems. Use redacted screenshots in this documentation.

## Follow the right path

| Situation | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| New app | Prepare source → submit enrollment YAML → validate/review → protected promotion → inspect provisioning and builds. |
| Already enrolled | Use the existing app identity and approved source triggers. Do not submit enrollment again. |
| Failed or uncertain operation | Preserve completed work and inspect actual state. Do not repeat an uncertain external write. |

Complete [Machine Setup](/mobile/onboarding/machine-setup-guide/) and [First Local Run](/mobile/onboarding/first-local-run/) before repository preparation.

