# Bitrise Pipelines, Parallel Tests & Limits

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing material, private artifacts, and sensitive logs in approved Enterprise systems. Examples use synthetic identities.

Use the approved catalog template. Application changes use the existing enrolled app; configuration `main` starts provisioning, not a routine app-source release.

## 1. Resolve the route to real native targets

| Route | Required mapping |
| :--- | :--- |
| `qa_android` | Approved QA variant → private APK → QA destination/audience. |
| `qa_ios` | Approved QA scheme/configuration → private IPA → QA destination/audience. |
| `uat_android` | Approved UAT variant → private APK → authorized UAT destination/audience. |
| `uat_ios` | Approved UAT scheme/configuration → private IPA → authorized UAT destination/audience. |

The handbook's `deploy-dev`, `deploy-staging-qa`, `release-prod`, and `pr-checks` are example workflow names, not replacements for the earlier four-route contract. CAMP environments, source branches, workflows, and delivery routes need an explicit catalog mapping.

## 2. Structure the approved stage-based pipeline

**`bitrise.yml` excerpt:** the hierarchy is pipelines → stages → workflows → steps. Stages run in order; workflows within a stage can run concurrently on isolated runners.

```yaml
pipelines:
  pr-pipeline:
    stages:
      - setup-and-lint: {}
      - test-modules-parallel: {}
      - build-smoke: {}
stages:
  setup-and-lint:
    workflows:
      - detect-and-lint: {}
  test-modules-parallel:
    workflows:
      - test-module-auth: {}
      - test-module-orders: {}
      - test-module-core: {}
  build-smoke:
    workflows:
      - compile-android-smoke: {}
      - compile-ios-smoke: {}
trigger_map:
  - pull_request_source_branch: "*"
    pipeline: pr-pipeline
```

Define every referenced workflow in the approved template. Add protected push/tag delivery triggers only from its confirmed mapping. Secret-bearing Danger work must use trusted tooling; a PR trigger does not authorize arbitrary PR code with release credentials.

The snippet uses the supplied stage model. Bitrise also supports graph pipelines with different dependency/condition placement; do not mix models or copy a root workflow `run_if` into an unsupported scope. See [Bitrise pipeline configuration](https://docs.bitrise.io/en/bitrise-ci/workflows-and-pipelines/build-pipelines/configuring-a-pipeline).

