> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing material, private artifacts, and sensitive logs in approved Enterprise systems. Examples use synthetic identities.

Platform-owned automation binds signing material. Developers configure compatible targets and inspect sanitized results; they do not upload raw production credentials manually.

## 1. Match credentials to their purpose

| Item | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- |
| Android keystore/key | Signs the selected APK/AAB. Alias, container password, and private-key password are distinct inputs. |
| Play upload identity | Can differ from the certificate Google Play uses for delivered APKs. |
| Apple certificate/private key and profile | Code signing for the app/extensions, team, entitlements, and distribution method. |
| App Store Connect `.p8` API key | Authorizes supported API operations; does not replace the signing key/profile. |
| Google Play service account | Authorizes store API operations; does not sign the binary. |
| App Management binding | Performs downstream distribution signing where the route requires it. |

No raw secrets or credential references go into enrollment YAML. CAMP's source-defined configuration-key names are a separate metadata contract.

