# Delivery & Release Verification

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing material, private artifacts, and sensitive logs in approved Enterprise systems. Examples use synthetic identities.

Deliver an identified candidate only after required tests, security, signing, and release authorization. Completion means the **intended version is available to the intended audience**, not merely uploaded.

## 1. Select the destination

| Destination | Required preparation |
| :--- | :--- |
| Enterprise App Management | Correct environment/app, signing binding, enabled version, approved assignment, user endpoint verification. |
| Google Play Internal Testing | Existing store record, package/version/signing, authorized service account, track and tester setup. |
| App Store Connect/TestFlight | Existing app record, API connection, signed IPA, version/build, processing/compliance and tester access. |
| Public production | Separate authorization, destination review/publication, and rollout controls. |

The source's first-time Play upload and account/API setup belong to **App Store & Distribution** and its authorized owners. Confirm prerequisites there before automation; do not give every developer store administration or raw JSON/Apple keys.

## 2. Validate the handoff

```bash
