Use the signed AAB output and actual approved package. The source's `user_fraction: 1.0` is not added blindly to an Internal Testing release; staged rollout controls belong to the selected track/status contract. `status: completed` is a mutation requesting availability under store rules, not a preview.

Confirm uploaded version code, intended track/state, processing/review restrictions, tester eligibility/opt-in, and exact-version access. Play App Signing can produce delivered APKs with different bytes/signing identity from the uploaded AAB. See the [Google Play Deploy contract](https://github.com/bitrise-steplib/steps-google-play-deploy).

