## 4. Apply all seven evidence milestones

| Milestone | Evidence |
| :--- | :--- |
| `BuildStarted` | Actual source commit/branch, route, workflow, template and inputs. |
| `BuildSuccessful` | Identified configured build completed successfully. |
| `ArtifactValidated` | Non-zero package, correct type/identity, hash and gate associations. |
| `Uploaded` | Authoritative destination receipt/version identity. |
| `Signed` | Required native/downstream signature and expected identity. |
| `Enabled` | Destination-specific required active/available state. |
| `Assigned & UserVisible` | Approved audience and exact-version visibility through the intended user's endpoint. |

These are evidence categories, not universal chronological signing order. Installation/launch is separate if acceptance requires it. An uploaded object awaiting signing/enablement is a **Provisional Upload Checkpoint**, never a completed release. Missing assignment/visibility also leaves delivery incomplete.

**Example evidence record — documentation-owned, not an API schema:**

