# Troubleshooting & Safe Recovery

> **Confidential — internal use only.** Keep credentials, signing material, private artifacts, and sensitive logs in approved Enterprise systems. Examples use synthetic identities.

Find the exact failed operation before rerunning a workflow. A red build can still have created an app, uploaded a binary, or completed another route.

## 1. Separate local failure from uncertain external state

| Observation | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| Validation/compilation failed before any external write | Correct the bounded source/configuration issue and rerun the relevant checks. |
| External operation returned a failure | Inspect whether partial effects remain before any recovery. |
| Timeout/lost response/interruption | Stop writes; result may already exist. Perform read-only reconciliation. |
| One route succeeded and another failed | Preserve the successful route; reconcile only unresolved work. |
| Destination is processing | Observe within the approved budget; do not upload again to accelerate it. |

The source contains conflicting retry guidance: earlier controlled retry, later one-write, and the new Sauce 2s/4s/8s backoff claim. **Do not blindly retry an uncertain mutation.** Safe read retries and provably unsent requests need the actual adapter's contract; a generic retry loop is not adopted.

<MermaidZoom title="Recovery: determine state before continuing remaining work">

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["Stop writes and preserve evidence"] --> B["Authorized read-only reconciliation"]
    B --> C["Identify completed and unresolved work"]
    C --> D["Reviewed remaining action and verification"]
    classDef step fill:#312e81,stroke:#a5b4fc,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef pass fill:#064e3b,stroke:#6ee7b7,color:#fff,stroke-width:2px;
    class A,B,C step;
    class D pass;
```

</MermaidZoom>

## 2. Preserve identifiers and inspect safely

Record app, source/configuration commits, route/build, artifact hash, destination version, correlation ID, completed operations, and first failed boundary. Do not copy leaked credentials into the evidence record.

```bash
git status --short --branch
git rev-parse --show-toplevel
git rev-parse HEAD
git branch --show-current
```

For an existing authorized artifact:

```bash
set -euo pipefail
: "${MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT:?Existing selected artifact required}"
test -s "$MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT"
shasum -a 256 "$MOBILE_EXISTING_ARTIFACT"
```

These commands do not establish remote truth. A local HEAD can differ from the build's actual commit; a local hash can differ after downstream signing.

## 3. Reconcile the actual operation

Use the service's documented GET/read-only adapter. Match environment, app/version, source/build, and operation/correlation evidence. Inspect processing, signing, enablement, assignment, and intended-user access as applicable.

| Readback | Decision |
| :--- | :--- |
| Correct existing result confirmed | Use/reconcile it; do not create/upload again. |
| Pending or inconclusive | Continue bounded observation or escalate. |
| Not found once | Not conclusive: check permissions, region, pagination/filter, processing and eventual consistency. |
| Absence conclusively established | Owner-reviewed recovery decision; no automatic replay authorization. |

Do not delete/recreate the app, replay protected merges, reset cursors, or replace signing credentials as an assumed repair. A recovery action must preserve verified work and comply with one-write policy. An uncertain recovery attempt stops again for readback.

## 4. Diagnose the failing boundary

| Symptom | Inspect | Avoid |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Request rejected | Canonical path/name, schema version, supported template/platform, secret/mutation fields. | Inventing fields or parallel filename variants. |
| CAMP rejected | Flat/nested version, actual consumer, native IDs, provisioned fields. | Mixing v1/v2/legacy schemas. |
| Vela preview missing | Current PR head, pending status, event association, approved operator/VPN access. | Treating unavailable evidence as passing. |
| Source/registry authentication | Actual binding, permission, source/ref and network. | Personal tokens embedded in URLs or TLS bypass. |
| Danger fails | Current metadata, trusted code, approved threshold, bot binding, required status. | Weakening rules or exposing the token to PR code. |
| Android signing | Selected artifact, alias/password, URL versus local path, expected certificate. | Debug-key fallback or key regeneration. |
| iOS signing/export | App/extension identity, team, profile/private key, entitlements and export method. | Assuming a valid API key proves code signing. |
| Sauce 401/404 | Credential binding, exact region/ID, receipt/access and job/package mapping. | Automatic key rotation or duplicate upload. |
| Sauce allocation/empty suite | Matrix/capacity, packaged tests, filters, actual discovery and reports. | Calling queue/no tests a pass. |
| NowSecure blocked/pending | Exact assessed binary, assessment completion, findings and policy. | Lowering threshold, suppressing findings, or treating submission as completion. |
| Exit 137 / ENOSPC | Runner timeout/memory logs, actual disk/stack budget. | Assuming every SIGKILL is a 90-minute timeout. |
| Store upload error | Package/version, actual acceptance/processing, authorization and request correlation. | Immediate re-upload after ambiguous transport. |
| User sees old/no version | Environment, enabled state, audience/entitlement, tester eligibility and exact version. | Assigning everyone or recreating the app. |

Read-only runner diagnostics:

```bash
df -h .
xcodebuild -version
```

Use Xcode commands only on the actual macOS build environment. Do not print the whole environment, raw tokens, profile contents, private artifact URLs, or account records.

## 5. Understand the workshop partial failure

The 28 October 2026 reference created the app and validated private artifacts. QA Android was signed, enabled, assigned and user-visible. QA iOS built, then App Management reported `distribution_signing_failed`; UAT publication was not confirmed.

Preserve QA Android and reconcile QA iOS. The issue was accepted as known for that exercise; the evidence does not establish a root cause or a certificate-replacement recipe.

## 6. Escalate with a short useful record

```markdown
# CI/CD failure
- App, route, environment and intended destination:
- Actual build commit / configuration merge / template version:
- Execution, correlation and destination references:
- Failed operation and sanitized error:
- Confirmed completed steps and successful routes:
- Read-only reconciliation result:
- Still pending/unknown:
- Preserved resources and requested owner decision:
- Authorized remaining action and observed outcome:
```

Use the approved Teams support channel; it is not itself authorization to rerun. Credential/data exposure follows the incident process. Production binary fixes use the approved roll-forward/versioning procedure; a destination change does not automatically replace installed binaries on every device.

