## Step 13 — Understand later builds

Recurring distribution reuses the enrolled app and durable candidate/route cursor. It does not repeat enrollment. On interruption, reconcile the in-flight operation before resuming remaining work. Do not trigger an extra build solely for demonstration outside the facilitator's scope.

## Step 14 — Handle partial failure

Stop writes and preserve app/source access, credentials, versions, artifacts and successful routes. Have Platform Engineering perform read-only reconciliation. Record the reviewed remaining action; do not reenroll, delete resources, retry an uncertain upload, or replace signing material as a guess.

The 28 October 2026 reference showed QA Android signed/enabled/assigned/user-visible; QA iOS built but failed downstream with `distribution_signing_failed`; UAT publication was unconfirmed. Overall: **partial failure**. Its underlying signing cause was not established. Preserve Android and reconcile iOS.

